  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Arbitration Council Foundation Cambodia 2014-2018</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Medlingsinstitut f&#xF6;r arbetsmarknaden i Kambodja 14-18</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Arbitration Council Foundation har ans&#xF6;kt om st&#xF6;d fr&#xE5;n Sida om 10.8 miljoner SEK f&#xF6;r institutets verksamhet under &#xE5;ren 2014-2018. Insatsen syftar till att fr&#xE4;mja en milj&#xF6; f&#xF6;r effektiv arbetsmarknadsstyrning f&#xF6;r den privata sektorn samt social utveckling genom att tillhandah&#xE5;lla ett v&#xE4;lfungerande och trov&#xE4;rdigt system f&#xF6;r medling i arbetsmarknadskonflikter. Insatsen har tre huvudm&#xE5;l:
1. tillhandah&#xE5;lla ett effektivt system f&#xF6;r medling i arbetsmarknadskonflikter som arbetstagare, arbetsgivare och allm&#xE4;nheten har f&#xF6;rtroende f&#xF6;r
2. &#xF6;ka kunskap om Arbitration Council och fr&#xE4;mja f&#xF6;rhandlingskapacitet hos arbetstagare och arbetsgivare genom kunskapsfr&#xE4;mjande &#xE5;tg&#xE4;rder, partnerskap och ut&#xE5;triktad verksamhet
3. vidmakth&#xE5;lla och fortsatt fr&#xE4;mja Arbitration Councils institutionella integritet och h&#xE5;llbarhet. 

Konsultation med Sida/JUR har skett. Sidas bidrag till Arbitration Council Foundation:s verksamhet &#xE4;r 10.8 miljoner kronor.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Arbitration Council foundation has submitted a proposal to Sida on project support to the Foundation for 2014-2018. The aim of the intervention is to promote an effective labour market governance environment for private sector and social development through the provision of a well-functioning and credible labour dispute arbitration system. The intervention has three main objectives: (1) providing effective labour dispute resolution services in which workers and employers, and the public have confidence, (2) raising awareness about the Arbitration Council and promote dispute resolution skills of workers and employers through increased capacity building and partnerships and stakeholder outreach activities, and (3) maintaining and promoting institutional integrity and sustainability of the Arbitration Council. The total Sida budget requested is SEK 10.8 million.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To contribute to an effective labour market governance environment for private sector and social development by enhancing the extent to which a well-functioning labour arbitration system builds workers&#x2019; and employers&#x2019; confidence that labour disputes will be resolved effectively and fairly.</narrative>
  </description>
